The options are:

enum CgroupOprions {
  MEMORY = 0;
  CPU = 1;
  IO = 2;
}


Sure, I just wanted to make those options  flexible but they can move to only server.

1. we transition the client from reading the log history to waiting by reading the []byte that is being written by Cmd output io.writer. we read it all and sent it as first value in channel and then transition to channel. of course we will lock the byte array when it's being read.
2. if the process is completed, there won't be any new value added to []byte so we won't receive any new value. We can check the status of the job periodically  during stream and end stream if process is ended.
3. each user will read the stream in a new goroutine. the index will initiate for each user on staring stream so with proper mutex usage multiple users can stream the same process.


```go
go func() {
...
		for {
			select {
			case <-ctx.Done():
				...
			default:
				

				mu.Lock()
				ln := len(so.data)
				

				var chunk []byte

				if ln > 0 {
					if firstScan {
						chunk = so.data[:ln]
						firstScan = false
					} else {
						chunk = so.data[pointer:ln]
					}
					pointer = ln
				}
				if len(chunk) > 0 {
					log := string(chunk)
					logChan <- log
				}
                                mu.Unlock()
                         }
		}
	}()
```

